# Provenance Audit Report — 25 coins — 2026-10-15

## Summary
Audited 25 coins with the weakest provenance (AI-level certainty on verifiable facts).
- 23 mintage verifications
- 2 composition verifications

## Key Findings

### C042/C044 (USSR 1 kopek 1962/1974) — SOURCE CORRECTION
The mintages (750,000,000 and 780,000,000) are CORRECT but were misattributed to Numista N#767.
Numista does not list per-year mintages for this type. The numbers come from the numisview
"Soviet Union 1 Kopek (Reform) Checklist" which lists them explicitly. Source corrected.

### All other mintages — CONFIRMED
23 mintages verified against Numista catalogue pages. All match the recorded values.
Provenance upgraded from AI-level to reference-level with exact N# citations.

### Compositions — CONFIRMED
- C273 (Germany 2005 1c): Copper plated steel (standard euro cent)
- C268 (Norway 2000 50 ore): Copper-nickel per Numista N#1442

## Methodology
- Compared each recorded value against the Numista catalogue page for that type/year
- For USSR coins, used numisview checklist (Numista lacks per-year data)
- All sources include exact N# and URL for Claude to verify

